@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.4.0
@changelog
  - Codename: You've Got to Haggle!
  - New: reasixty.com is live — the extension's home on the web, generated from the repo, with no tracking and no external hosts. Manual, features, install, about.
  - New: Mapping Exchange — share and install plug-in mappings (UC1 / UF8 / UC1+UF8) from inside REAPER (Settings -> Exchange) or on the web. Browse by plug-in with a coverage figure and a "works for me" vote; publish with one click from the FX-Learn Share dialog; passkey / magic-link sign-in; CC0; mappings only, never setup bundles.
  - Learn: Fill Sequential now steps the scribble label with the parameter ("Ch 1" -> "Ch 16"), fader + V-Pot, in both the Settings editor and the Learn-HUD.
  - Learn-HUD: the UF8 colour bars are clickable — left-click picks a strip's colour, right-click fills all eight strips of the active bank.
  - FX-Learn: tap Ctrl / Opt / Ctrl+Opt to switch the schematic to that overlay's mapping, tap the same combo again to return to Normal.
  - FX-Learn: params bound in the UC1 EXT FUNCS menu now show as bound in the parameter list instead of looking free to grab.
